      "_key": "!actors.items!n5elvxF09A0csTLT.n5etYTn1Dj1mbelk",
      "name": "Flying Mount",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>The Clay Birds primary purpose is to be a flying mount. A creature of your choice can mount the Clay Bird. When it does, replace the creatures movement with the Clay Birds. The Clay Bird moves with the mounted creature. If you are mounted to the Clay Bird, you cannot command it to move separate from you unless you dismount by spending 5 feet of your normal movement. Attacks targeting the mounted Creature does not harm the Clay Bird and attacks targeting the Clay Bird does not harm the mounted creature. A mounted creature can spend its reaction to switch targets causing either themselves or the Clay Bird to interpose an attack targeting the other. Effects that target an area affects both the Clay Bird and mounted creature as individuals.</p>",
        "category": "npcTraits",
